Z||000000||NewAgeFiero||11-07-2001||08:46 PM||||I am looking to buy an 85 gt fiero. i need to know: the difference in a notchback, and a fastback, what is the biggest rims a fiero can fit comfortably, do many gt's come with a turbo, where can you buy turbo's for fieros, and how much of a hlep is nos?||||reg||5
Z||000001||dennis_6||11-07-2001||08:55 PM||||I will try to answer some of you questions.<BR>A notchback and a fastback are only cosmetic differences.  If you want to see a fastback look at the fiero next to the Pennocks Fiero Forum title.  No Fiero ever came factory with a turbo.  NOS would be much cheaper and easier to install than a turbo.  You can get a turbo from Design One Systems.  Hope this helps.||||reg||10
Z||000002||GTFiero1||11-07-2001||09:35 PM||||NOS may blow your engine if you dont rebuild it properly with all forged components. turbo would be a nice way to go  <A HREF="http://www.designonesystems.com" TARGET=_blank>www.designonesystems.com</A>    also engine conversions are available too... <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com" TARGET=_blank>www.v8archie.com</A>    <A HREF="http://www.americancustomeng.com" TARGET=_blank>www.americancustomeng.com</A> <P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.||||reg||1
